1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,198
Sam has put this bowl

2
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:02,570
through the dishwasher twice.

3
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:05,450
It still looks like dinner is in progress.

4
00:00:05,740 --> 00:00:06,850
You had one job.

5
00:00:07,140 --> 00:00:08,690
And you gave me an obstacle course.

6
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:09,590
Two charges.

7
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:10,890
Wasting water.

8
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:12,130
Failing to wash.

9
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:13,170
How do you plead?

10
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:14,750
I'd like to question the loader.

11
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,438
Sam bought a machine to get

12
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:17,330
out of washing dishes.

13
00:00:17,760 --> 00:00:18,598
Now he's doing it

14
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:20,270
before the cycle and after.

15
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,130
Tonight, he's demanding a refund.

16
00:00:23,270 --> 00:00:24,108
The dishwasher requests

17
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:25,540
footage from last night.

18
00:00:25,970 --> 00:00:28,100
Sam stands at the sink, rinsing a plate.

19
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:28,840
Then another.

20
00:00:29,290 --> 00:00:30,360
The faucet keeps running.

21
00:00:30,510 --> 00:00:32,440
By the time each plate enters the machine,

22
00:00:32,670 --> 00:00:34,200
Sam has practically washed it.

23
00:00:34,590 --> 00:00:35,140
I'm helping.

24
00:00:35,570 --> 00:00:36,428
You hired a dishwasher

25
00:00:36,430 --> 00:00:37,960
and then did its shift.

26
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:40,060
I thought I had to get the food off first.

27
00:00:40,490 --> 00:00:41,648
Big scraps, yes.

28
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:43,520
The actual washing was my part.

29
00:00:43,630 --> 00:00:44,640
Check my instructions.

30
00:00:45,110 --> 00:00:46,380
We have a whole section on this.

31
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:47,948
A document this court suspects

32
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:49,240
has never been opened.

33
00:00:49,670 --> 00:00:50,520
You run for hours.

34
00:00:50,870 --> 00:00:52,040
How is that saving water?

35
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:55,610
Because I'm not a faucet running for hours.

36
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:57,550
Water collects at the bottom.

37
00:00:58,120 --> 00:00:59,910
A pump sends it through the spray arms.

38
00:01:00,680 --> 00:01:02,950
The water entering those arms is filtered.

39
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,758
Hot water, detergent,

40
00:01:04,760 --> 00:01:06,530
and moving jets do the cleaning.

41
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:09,638
Later, the dirty water drains away

42
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,190
and fresh water rinses the dishes.

43
00:01:11,620 --> 00:01:12,818
The court watches a cutaway.

44
00:01:12,820 --> 00:01:14,538
This machine doesn't fill

45
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:16,090
to the roof like a bathtub.

46
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:18,258
And rinsing every plate at the sink adds

47
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:20,530
water use before its cycle even starts.

48
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:21,250
Fine.

49
00:01:21,520 --> 00:01:22,910
Then explain the dirty bowl.

50
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:25,360
The rack rolls forward.

51
00:01:25,670 --> 00:01:27,440
Two bowls are tucked tightly together.

52
00:01:27,870 --> 00:01:29,840
The dirty one is hiding inside the other.

53
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:31,168
How was the spray supposed

54
00:01:31,170 --> 00:01:32,480
to reach that surface?

55
00:01:32,910 --> 00:01:33,720
I was saving space.

56
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:36,240
You also saved that bowl from being washed.

57
00:01:36,670 --> 00:01:37,680
Sam separates them.

58
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:40,088
For the first time, the inside of the bowl

59
00:01:40,090 --> 00:01:42,120
has an open path toward the spray.

60
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:44,040
And the obstacle course?

61
00:01:44,470 --> 00:01:46,488
With the machine off, Sam gently

62
00:01:46,490 --> 00:01:48,120
turns the lower spray arm.

63
00:01:48,430 --> 00:01:50,128
It bumps into a long utensil

64
00:01:50,130 --> 00:01:51,260
hanging below the rack.

65
00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:52,288
Sam moves it.

66
00:01:52,290 --> 00:01:53,940
The arm turns freely.

67
00:01:54,830 --> 00:01:55,980
That thing is supposed to move.

68
00:01:56,250 --> 00:01:57,380
You gave it a parking brake.

69
00:01:57,810 --> 00:01:58,608
The dishwasher looks

70
00:01:58,610 --> 00:01:59,840
ready to collect damages.

71
00:02:00,390 --> 00:02:02,100
Then Sam points beneath the rack.

72
00:02:02,490 --> 00:02:02,820
Hold on.

73
00:02:02,830 --> 00:02:03,680
What's in your filter?

74
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:06,298
Following the manual, Sam

75
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:07,730
removes this model's filter.

76
00:02:08,220 --> 00:02:09,378
It has caught food debris

77
00:02:09,380 --> 00:02:10,450
from earlier meals.

78
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:12,270
You were going to mention this when?

79
00:02:12,700 --> 00:02:12,918
I...

80
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:14,110
could use a cleaning.

81
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:15,618
Then we'll test the evidence

82
00:02:15,620 --> 00:02:16,810
instead of the attitude.

83
00:02:17,240 --> 00:02:18,318
Poor loading isn't

84
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,690
the only possible problem.

85
00:02:19,960 --> 00:02:21,510
This machine also needs care.

86
00:02:21,760 --> 00:02:23,058
And if cleaning stays poor

87
00:02:23,060 --> 00:02:24,470
after the recommended checks,

88
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,310
a real fault may need investigation.

89
00:02:27,180 --> 00:02:29,390
A dirty bowl alone doesn't settle that.

90
00:02:30,370 --> 00:02:33,048
Sam checks the manual, cleans the filter

91
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:35,520
as directed, and locks it back in place.

92
00:02:36,210 --> 00:02:38,400
This time, food scraps go in the trash.

93
00:02:39,070 --> 00:02:40,448
Ordinary leftovers don't

94
00:02:40,450 --> 00:02:41,660
get a full sink wash.

95
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:43,948
Stubborn or starchy messes get

96
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:45,920
the pretreatment the manual calls for.

97
00:02:46,310 --> 00:02:47,208
The bowls sit apart,

98
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:49,240
with their insides facing the spray.

99
00:02:49,930 --> 00:02:50,940
Nothing obstructs the arms.

100
00:02:51,850 --> 00:02:53,628
Sam adds detergent made for dishwashers

101
00:02:53,630 --> 00:02:55,260
and chooses the appropriate cycle.

102
00:02:55,650 --> 00:02:56,540
Court is in recess.

103
00:02:56,850 --> 00:02:57,860
Let the defendant work.

104
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:01,600
After the cycle, Sam opens the door.

105
00:03:01,970 --> 00:03:03,020
The bowl comes out clean.

106
00:03:03,650 --> 00:03:04,488
The judge checks it

107
00:03:04,490 --> 00:03:05,680
against the original photo.

108
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:06,800
Same bowl.

109
00:03:06,930 --> 00:03:08,100
A very different assignment.

110
00:03:08,490 --> 00:03:10,160
For this load, the complaint is dismissed.

111
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:11,960
So you actually can wash dishes?

112
00:03:12,390 --> 00:03:13,540
It's literally my name.
